@startuml
' Conceptual view: storage identifiers and EF details intentionally omitted.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
left to right direction
class Smurf {
  +Name : string {get; set;}
  +Age : int {get; set;}
}
class Village {
  +Name : string {get; set;}
}
class Pet {
  +Name : string {get; set;}
}
Village "0..1" --> "0..*" Smurf : Smurfs (accepted membership)
Smurf "0..*" --> "0..1" Pet : Pet
note bottom of Village
  Source exposes a mutable Smurfs collection only.
  Accepted: a Smurf belongs to zero or one village.
  No reverse Village navigation on Smurf, by decision.
  Plain collections do not enforce exclusive membership.
  EF tracks one optional village through a shadow FK;
  see the separate relational model.
end note
note bottom of Smurf
  Name assignments require non-whitespace text
  and at most 20 characters.
  Age has no range validation.
  Pet may be shared; no reverse collection on Pet.
end note
@enduml
